---
description: Rails 8 conventions for the sample todo app
alwaysApply: true
---
- One resource only: Todo model, TodosController, resources :todos in routes.rb
- Views live under app/views/todos/
- Use before_action :set_todo for show, edit, update, destroy
- Mutating actions (create, update, destroy) use respond_to with format.html and format.json
- HTML success redirects with flash notice; validation failures use status: :unprocessable_content
- Use params.expect for strong parameters, not require/permit
- Shared partials use leading underscores, stored in app/views/todos/
- Use form_with(model: todo) in forms — Turbo is enabled by default
- Use dom_id(todo) for stable DOM ids
- Frontend uses Turbo + Stimulus via importmap, no inline script tags in ERB
- No Bootstrap gem — Propshaft for assets
- SQLite only, schema scoped to a single todos table
- All schema changes go through reversible migrations, never hand-edit db/schema.rb
- Tests use Minitest under test/ — not RSpec
- No new gems without approval
- CSRF protection stays on, never use skip_before_action :verify_authenticity_token
